# Committed schedules (Phase 33).
#
# The schedule store writes one JSON document per committed timetable
# into `data/schedules/`. Those are OPERATIONAL DATA, not source: a
# committed schedule is a property of one school's deployment, it can
# be a few MB, and there is no merge semantics for a file whose
# contents depend on a local dataset. Committing them would put a
# machine's generated timetable into version control and make every
# commit noisy.
#
# The store RECREATES the directory on start, so deleting it loses
# committed schedules and nothing else. If a schedule must survive a
# clean checkout, copy the directory out before cleaning.
data/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Local env (`.env.example` IS tracked — it is the documented template)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/*
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Probe scripts written during ad-hoc investigation, kept out of the
# test glob by name rather than by deletion.
_probe_*.mjs
_load.mjs
